  "summary": "Eight preprints in November 2026 test sequence-to-function models on variant effects, long-read epigenomes, personal genomes and admixed cohorts.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is deep learning for predicting regulatory activity and variant effects from DNA sequence, with attention to where current models fall short. AlphaGenome 2 predicts cell-type-specific activity from 1-Mb sequences. ModBERT adds population variants and CpG methylation from long reads, while FiberTron trains a compact model on one sample's Fiber-seq and nanopore RNA-seq. LAMP examines why fine-tuning on personal genomes fails to improve expression prediction, linking this to distal effects, and a comparison in admixed Latino individuals evaluates fine-tuned Borzoi and AlphaGenome against variant-based methods. Related single-cell work, including MCT, DRAFT and CMC-VAE, models gene co-regulation, dynamic regulatory networks and causal structure with perturbation prediction.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-25"
